  - biofuels
  - Brazil
abstract: >-
  terrdiag is a Python library implementing a two-layer territorial diagnostic
  framework for longitudinal public policy metrics. Layer 1 builds entity-level
  (municipal) typologies via PCA and K-means on socio-environmental indicators,
  with bootstrap stability checks; Layer 2 applies global and local Moran's I
  (LISA) with distance-based spatial weights to point-level outcomes; the
  overlay cross-tabulates both layers into diagnostic cells that signal
  territorial tensions between structural typology and outcome dynamics.
  The package ships a reference data-preparation pipeline for Brazil's
  RenovaBio programme.
